h the glasses and smell the rose  petals she kept in an alabaster jar on  her table  she said that the rose petals were from  germany and the jar was from greece  one afternoon i was allowed to handle  the precious glasses and was looking out  at the street  i had a cab pulled up  and a tall skinny sailor got out  he shook hands with the cabbie who took  a sea bag from the trunk  and i knew that it was my uncle bill  home from the war  my grandmother came running down the  steps into his arms  she was crying  i remember the stars that hung in the  windows of some of our neighbors houses  my grandmother told me it was because  someone had lost his son in the war  i was glad that we didn't have any stars  in our windows  that night we had a huge celebration for  uncle bill  i went to sleep feeling glad that my  uncle was home safe  i didn't think about mr burnhauser  anymore  [Applause]  [Music]  i just wanted to thank you all for  coming it's been a wonderful night and  i'm glad you're all here thank you  readers and audience alike thank you so  much  [Applause]  i thought my father was god is published  by henry holton company for more  information visit their website  henryholt.com  next week on public lives a look at the  life of american public

